.TH HULLCHECK 1 "2026-10-25" "hullcheck 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hullcheck \- read-only security review for the SaaS you built with an AI agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hullcheck
[\fIPATH\fR] [\fB--json\fR] [\fB--exit-zero\fR] [\fB-h\fR] [\fB-V\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hullcheck
reads a repository and reports the common mistakes that leak data or money
(Supabase and Firebase rules, secrets in client code, unverified Stripe
webhooks, TLS verification turned off, unpinned or injectable GitHub Actions,
and more). Every finding quotes the exact file and line behind it, grouped into
the lanes Fix Now, Monitor, Validate Manually and Unverified.
.PP
It reads files only. It makes no network calls, writes nothing, runs no code
from the scanned repository, and never claims the application is secure.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B PATH
Repository to scan. Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable JSON instead of the human report.
.TP
.B --exit-zero
Always exit 0, even when there are Fix Now findings.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No Fix Now findings, or \fB--exit-zero\fR was given.
.TP
.B 1
At least one Fix Now finding.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage, or PATH is not a directory.
.SH IGNORING
A
.B .hullcheckignore
file at the repository root lists gitignore-style patterns to skip. An inline
.B hullcheck:ignore
comment silences one line, and
.B hullcheck:ignore-next-line
silences the line below it.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The full review kit: https://www.rettecnologia.org/promptbook
.SH AUTHOR
RET Tecnologia.
